@node WHAT_IS_PDC "What is PrO-DmScHeCk"
                     @{u}What is PrO-DmScHeCk ?@{uu}

PrO-DmScHeCk is a DMS file checker meant to be run from a BBS when a
DMS file has been uploaded.

It allows other BBS adverts to be stripped from the file, and your own
BBS adverts can be added to advertise your BBS.

PrO-DmScHeCk was written in 680x0 assembler using Devpac 3 from HiSoft.

PrO-DmScHeCk needs kickstart 2.0 or better installed on your Amiga in
order for it to run, if there is enough need (ie at least 10 people
wanting it) then I'll do a 1.3 compatible version.

@endnode

@node PDC_OPTS "PrO-DmScHeCk Options"
               @{u}PrO-DmScHeCk's command line options@{uu}

Usage : @{b}PrO-DmScHeCk@{ub} [<options>] <filename>

Where options is one or more of :

   @{b}BACK@{ub} - Add a tail banner (from @{b}S:PDC_Banner_Rear@{ub})

   @{b}FRONT@{ub} - Add a front banner (from @{b}S:PDC_Banner_Front@{ub})

   @{b}TRACK@{ub} - Add a track 0 banner (from @{b}S:PDC_Track_Zero@{ub}
                             this file @{b}MUST@{ub} be 960 bytes long.)

@{u}Option in the @{b}REGISTERED@{ub} version @{b}ONLY@{ub}@{uu}

   @{b}DATE@{ub} - Add the current time and/or date to one/all of the
                text to be added.

      When '##-###-###' appears in a file the date will be added,
       and when '##:##' appears the current time will be added.

@endnode

@node INSTALLATION "How to install PrO-DmScHeCk"
                    @{u}Installation instructions@{uu}

@{u}Installation for normal command line usage@{uu}

Copy @{b}PrO-DmScHeCk@{ub} to anywhere in your path (usually C:).

@{u}Installation for Ami-Express BBS usage@{uu}

Load Workbench and double click on the '@{b}Install_PLC@{ub} icon, or
open a shell and type '@{b}execute Install_PLC@{ub}'

Edit the files @{b}S:PDC_Banner_Front@{ub} (any size),
               @{b}S:PDC_Banner_Rear@{ub} (any size)
           and @{b}S:PDC_Track_Zero@{ub} (960 bytes)

 to suit your own BBS.

Now when a DMS file is uploaded it will be automatically checked for
validity and integrity by PrO-DmScHeCk.
@endnode

