@node HISTORY "The history of PrO-DmScHeCk"
                     @{u}History of PrO-DmScHeCk@{uu}

| Ver   | Date          | Comment
+-------+---------------+--------------------------------------------
| 1.0   | 15-Jun-94     | First version.
+-------+---------------+--------------------------------------------
| 1.1   | 18-Jun-94     | Fixed a problem making the backup file in
|       |               | case of an error.
|       |               | Improved the speed of the checking.
+-------+---------------+--------------------------------------------
| 2.0   | 21-Jun-94     | Total re-write due to :
|       |               |  @{b}o@{ub} 1.1 corrupted DMS files on 68030
|       |               |  @{b}o@{ub} Was a lot slower than Mapus.
|       |               | As a consequence of the re-write :
|       |               |  @{b}o@{ub} Code is a @{b}LOT@{ub} smaller.
|       |               |  @{b}o@{ub} Now 20% faster than Mapus.
+-------+---------------+--------------------------------------------
| 2.01  | 22-Jun-94     | Fixed a bug that caused it not to add texts
|       |               | even though it could have been able to.
|       |               | Now displays banners and track zero's when
|       |               | the file is unpacked with DMS versions
|       |               | below 2.0
+-------+---------------+--------------------------------------------
| 2.1   | 03-Jul-94     | Now kickstart 2.0 only, a 68000 version
|       |               |  (reg. users only). Fixed a bug that caused
|       |               |  PDC to fail on multi-node BBS's.
+-------+---------------+--------------------------------------------
@endnode

@node OTHER_PROGS "Other programs that I have written"
         @{u}Here is a list of other programs that I have written@{uu}

@{b}BootUte@{ub}        : Degrader type utility for @{i}newer@{ui} Amiga's....
                 Needs Kickstart 2.0+. Features easy to use gadtools
                 interface.

@{b}BullRead@{ub}       : Bulletins door for /X that allows users to search
                 bulletins while they are on-line, or download the bulletins
                 for viewing whilst off-line.

@{b}X-Zippy@{ub}        : Replacement zippy search door for /X that can search
                 for multiple items at a time, about 3 times faster
                 than the built in zippy!!

@{b}UserCom@{ub}        : Door for /X that allows users to make comments to files
                 so that others will know if the file is old, fake etc.

@{b}PrO-DmScHeCk@{ub}   : DMS file checker - for user with most BBS systems.
                 Strips and adds front, rear and track texts.

@{b}PrO-LhAcHeCk@{ub}   : LHa file checker - for user with most BBS systems.
                 Strips most other adverts and adds own adverts that are
                 virtually unstrippable.

@{b}PrO-LogInfo@{ub}    : An Ami-Express door to inform on-line users when another
                 user logs on to, or off from, another node.

@{b}Decrunch@{ub}       : CLI based decruncher to decrunch loads of different
                 packed files.

@{b}PPPatch@{ub}        : PowerPacker Patcher... Patches the headers of PowerPacked
                 files so that they can't be decrunched.

@{u}Projects I'm working on@{uu}

@{b}BootUte 2@{ub}      : Updated version of BootUte.

@{b}EBBS@{ub}           : En¿gma Bulletin Board System
                 My own host BBS, written entirely in Assembler with loads
                 of features : Kickstart 2.0+ only.

@{b}PrO-MuLtIcHeCk@{ub} : Multiple file checker for most BBS systems, will
                 incorporate PrO-DmScHeCk and PrO-LhAcHeCk, along with a
                 text checker/adder.

@{b}PrO-NewScan@{ub}    : Ami-Express new file scanner, like Turbo-NewScan,
                 only faster!!

@{b}PrO-NewUser@{ub}    : Ami-Express new user questionnaire door that doesn't
                 let new users skip questions, they have to insert something
                 'intelligent', eg phone numbers can only have certain
                 characters in them..

@{b}<xxxx>Asm@{ub}      : 680x0 assembler with loads of features.
                 The assembler is going to be written by me, and Oll¿e is
                 writing a cool editor for it, with some excellent features.
                 (note <xxxx>Asm as I have thought of a name, yet!)

If you have any suggestions for features that you would like to see in
any of the programs then e-mail me with your suggestions.

@endnode
